  "term": "deviation",
  "definition": "Deviation is a turning away from a usual or given position. In this historical usage, it especially refers to abnormal turning of the eyes, including a persistent turning of both eyes to one side or the misalignment that can occur when one eye muscle is paralyzed; this may lead to double vision.",
